/**
\mainpage iccDEV Documentation

iccDEV provides C++ libraries and command-line tools for ICC.1 and ICC.2/iccMAX
color profiles. Start with the guides, or choose a reference area below. The
Namespaces, Classes, and Files tabs provide source-level API indexes.

- \ref curateddocumentation "Get started" - install, use, and build iccDEV.
- \ref curatedlibraries "Libraries" - four public C++ libraries and their API guides.
- \ref curatedtools "Tools" - command-line guides and processing diagrams.
- \ref curatedexamples "Examples" - sample applications.
- \ref curatedmaintainerqa "Maintainer QA" - workflows, test guides, and reports.
*/

/**
\page curateddocumentation Get Started

- \subpage md_docs_2using-iccdev "Using iccDEV"
- \subpage md_docs_2install "Install"
- \subpage md_docs_2build "Build"
*/

/**
\page curatedlibraries Libraries

Choose a library to find its public headers and related guides. These are the
four exported C++ libraries; the names in parentheses are their CMake targets.
`IccXML2` requires `ENABLE_ICCXML`; `IccJSON2` and `IccConnect2` require
`ENABLE_ICCJSON`.

- \subpage curatedproflib "IccProfLib (IccProfLib2)"
- \subpage curatedxmllib "IccXML / IccLibXML (IccXML2)"
- \subpage curatedjsonlib "IccJSON / IccLibJSON (IccJSON2)"
- \subpage curatedconnectlib "IccConnect / IccLibConnect (IccConnect2)"
*/

/**
\page curatedproflib IccProfLib

The core library reads, writes, applies, and validates ICC.1 and ICC.2/iccMAX
profiles. Link the `IccProfLib2` target. Start with the \ref IccProfile.h
"profile API", \ref IccCmm.h "color-management API", and \ref IccTag.h
"tag API".

- \subpage md_docs_2c-api-validation "C validation API"
- \subpage md_docs_2icc-cmm-threading "Parallel CMM apply"
- \subpage md_docs_2pcs-adjustment-placement "PCS adjustment placement"
*/

/**
\page curatedxmllib IccXML / IccLibXML

The XML library converts profiles and their tags to and from XML. Link the
`IccXML2` target. See \ref IccProfileXml.h "profile XML",
\ref IccTagXml.h "tag XML", and \ref IccMpeXml.h "multi-process element XML"
for the source-level API. The \ref md_IccXML_2CmdLine_2IccToXml_2Readme
"iccToXml" and \ref md_IccXML_2CmdLine_2IccFromXml_2Readme "iccFromXml"
guides cover the command-line tools.
*/

/**
\page curatedjsonlib IccJSON / IccLibJSON

The JSON library converts profiles and their tags to and from JSON. Link the
`IccJSON2` target. See \ref IccProfileJson.h "profile JSON" and
\ref IccTagJson.h "tag JSON" for the source-level API.

- \subpage md_docs_2iccjson "Working with ICC profiles using IccJSON"
- \subpage md_docs_2iccjson-tag-types "ICC JSON tag types"
*/

/**
\page curatedconnectlib IccConnect / IccLibConnect

The Connect library constructs initialized CMMs from JSON-driven
configuration. Link the `IccConnect2` target. See \ref IccConnect.h
"CMM factory" and \ref IccCmmConfig.h "configuration API".

- \subpage md_docs_2icc-connect "IccConnect library guide"
*/

